<div class="blog-wrap">
  <h1>Sponsor the project</h1>
  <p class="blog-intro">Health Flare and Inner Flare are free, open source, and built by one developer. No ads, no data to sell, no investors to answer to. If that's worth keeping around, sponsoring is the most direct way to help.</p>

  <aside class="use-case-cta" aria-labelledby="sponsor-cta-heading">
    <h2 id="sponsor-cta-heading">GitHub Sponsors</h2>
    <p>The goal is five monthly sponsors. That alone would cover the domains, hosting, and store fees that keep both apps running, while keeping the project cost-neutral.</p>
    <p class="use-case-stores">
      <a href="https://github.com/sponsors/Health-Flare" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sponsor on GitHub ↗</a>
    </p>
  </aside>

  <h2>More ways to give</h2>
  <p>These aren't set up yet. If GitHub Sponsors doesn't work for you, say so in an issue on the <a href="https://github.com/Health-Flare/website/issues">website repo</a>; it helps decide what to build next.</p>
  <ul class="coming-soon-list">
    <li class="coming-soon-card">
      <div>
        <h3>Open Collective</h3>
        <p>Transparent, pooled funding with public expenses, for sponsors who want visibility into where the money goes.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="coming-soon-badge">Coming soon</span>
    </li>
    <li class="coming-soon-card">
      <div>
        <h3>Ko-fi</h3>
        <p>A lower-friction way to give a one-time amount, without creating a GitHub account.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="coming-soon-badge">Coming soon</span>
    </li>
    <li class="coming-soon-card">
      <div>
        <h3>Employer matching</h3>
        <p>Many companies match employee donations to open source projects. Documentation for matching programs is on the way.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="coming-soon-badge">Coming soon</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Not ready to sponsor?</h2>
  <p>Most of what this project needs isn't money. See <a href="https://github.com/Health-Flare/.github/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">ways to help</a> for design, testing, writing, and clinical review, or just <a href="https://github.com/Health-Flare">browse the code</a>. Everyone who helps is credited on the <a href="/thanks/">thanks page</a>.</p>
</div>
